gcp-jxtc landed as 16f92c8 (1559 -> 1748 lines). Re-checked both findings
against the merged tree instead of carrying them forward on assumption; all
line references updated.

Both hold, and one is strengthened: jxtc added a FOURTH DECIDED_LAST rollback
site (:1653, the removal-reserve refusal). Correct per candidate, but the
cross-cycle effect runs the wrong way — the tighter the budget, the more
candidates roll back, so the cursor advances least exactly when starvation is
worst. Bead B's advance must key on what a cycle ENUMERATED, not what it
disposed of.

Also bounds Bead A honestly: the roster read at :945 is a direct
gc session list with no bare-bd equivalent, so only the two bead reads can be
cheapened. Expected recovery ~2 fixed-overhead units, not the whole budget.

Records the pin caveat: the city still pins 2583963 (1079-line reaper, 23
commits back), so every operational number in the doc came from a different
script than the one being patched. Do not validate against live reaper logs.

